            "result_text": "I've written a comprehensive regex pattern to `/app/regex.txt`. Here's how it works:\n\n**Pattern Structure:**\n- `^(?=.*IPv4)` - Lookahead ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n- `.*?(date)` - Matches the last date on the line (using non-greedy `.*?` with a greedy negative lookahead)\n- `(?!.*date)` - Negative lookahead ensures no more dates follow this one\n\n**IPv4 Component:**\n- Each octet: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9][0-9]|[0-9])` \n- Matches 0-255 without leading zeros (prevents \"001.002.003.004\")\n- Word boundaries: `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])`\n\n**Date Component (YYYY-MM-DD):**\n- 31-day months (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days 01-31\n- 30-day months (04,06,09,11): days 01-30  \n- February: days 01-29 (allowing leap years in any year as specified)\n- Word boundaries prevent matching strings like \"1134-12-1234\"\n\nThe regex with `re.MULTILINE` will correctly:\n- Skip lines without IPv4 addresses\n- Find only the last date on lines that have IPv4 addresses\n- Avoid false matches from adjacent alphanumeric characters"
